<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances rise in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances rise in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances rose in the week that ended June 11, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					Wk to Ju 11  Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  27.76   -0.065    +1.101</p>
<p>Government cash 6alances	     4.67   +0.816    -2.161</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	461.19   -0.957    -5.262</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 124.40   -1.400   -40.700</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.41   -0.054    +1.984</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>					   Apr 97     Mar 97     Apr 96</p>
<p>M1					  69.62	68.47	60.17</p>
<p>M2					 391.14     391.44     391.13</p>
<p>M3					 503.50     505.61     478.75</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			April	 March</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-17.29	-16.80</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     707.80	705.60</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    105.66	108.03</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
